        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Adjectival Clause: Adjectival clauses modify nouns. Also called relative clauses, they usually begin with a relative pronoun: which, that, whom, whose, who. There are two kinds: restrictive and nonrestrictive.",
